:: A6_start
<<set $act to 6>><<spend 12>>
<blockquote>The stairs go up and up. The wood cries under your feet. Wind screams through the holes in the walls. Below you, Florence is a field of tiny lights.</blockquote>

Halfway up, the stairs are broken. There is a big gap.

[[Jump the gap|A6_jump]]
[[Climb the old bell rope|A6_rope]]
[[Climb the outside wall|A6_wall]]

:: A6_jump
<<spend 2>>
You run and jump. Your fingers catch the edge. You pull yourself up.

But your candle falls. Down, down, into the dark.

<<if $satchel.includes("flint")>>You have the flint from the window. You find the candle on a beam and light it again.

[[Climb on|A6_top]]
<<else>>You climb down in the dark to find it. It takes a long time. The wax runs.

<<spend 8>>[[Climb on|A6_top]]
<</if>>

:: A6_rope
<<spend 6>>
The rope is old but strong. You climb slowly, hand over hand.

Your arms burn. The candle in your teeth drips hot wax on your chin.

It takes a long time. But you are safe.

[[Climb on|A6_top]]

:: A6_wall
<<spend 4>>
Outside, the wind tries to pull you off the wall. You do not look down.

Then you do look down. On the hill, grey robes. Many of them. Coming up.

[[Climb on|A6_top]]

:: A6_top
<<spend 2>>
<blockquote>Above you, the great bell waits. Black and silent, like a sleeping giant.</blockquote>

Next to it is an old wooden box. On the lid is Leonardo's sign.

Inside: folded wings of wood and cloth. A note: //For my student. For the way down.//

<<set $flags.has_wings to true>>
[[Go to the bell|A6_bell]]

:: A6_bell
<<spend 1>>
There is a bird-shaped hole in the bell. Over it, one word in mirror writing:

<div class="mirror">EVOL</div>

Say the word as you turn the key.

<<textbox "_guess" "">>
<<link "Turn the bird key">><<mirror _guess "love" "A6_book" "A6_bell_wrong">><</link>>

:: A6_bell_wrong
<<spend 3>>
The key will not turn. Read it from right to left. L, then O, then V, then E.

[[Try again|A6_bell]]

:: A6_book
The bell opens like a flower.

Inside is the book. You hold it for the first time. It is warm, like a living thing.

It opens by itself to a page about love.

<<if $heart gte 6>><<speak "love">><<else>>The page stays blank. The book does not trust you. Not yet.<</if>>

[[Close the book|A6_end]]

:: A6_end [autosave]
<<spend 2>>
"Beautiful, is it not?"

The Grey Abbot stands at the top of the stairs. $captive is beside him, tied with rope.

He smiles kindly.

//"Now we talk."//

[[Face him|A7_start]]
